    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A sudden, massive flood of greens is unlikely to \"reset\" your system safely while on warfarin. These high levels of Vitamin K can cause unpredictable fluctuations in your INR, which is dangerous for heart health. Instead of a two-week overload, focus on integrating a moderate, diverse serving of greens into every meal consistently. Your doctor's guidance is the most critical factor for safely optimizing your diet while on anticoagulants.",
      "source": "target",
